<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A particle moves along a straight line with displacement <m>s = {t^3-6 t^2+9 t}</m> metres after <m>t</m> seconds. For each time, describe the motion.</p><div>At <m>t = {0.5}</m> s: [ positive direction, speeding up | positive direction, slowing down | negative direction, speeding up | negative direction, slowing down ]  </div><div>At <m>t = {1.5}</m> s: [ positive direction, speeding up | positive direction, slowing down | negative direction, speeding up | negative direction, slowing down ]  </div><div>At <m>t = {4}</m> s: [ positive direction, speeding up | positive direction, slowing down | negative direction, speeding up | negative direction, slowing down ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The sign of <m>v</m> gives the direction of motion. The particle is speeding up when <m>v</m> and <m>a</m> have the same sign (pulling the same way), and slowing down when their signs differ.</p><p><m>v = \dfrac{ds}{dt} = {3 t^2-12 t+9}</m> and <m>a = \dfrac{dv}{dt} = {6 t-12}</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>t</m> (s)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>v</m> (m/s)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>a</m> (m/s<m>^2</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Signs of <m>v</m>, <m>a</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Motion</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\displaystyle {\frac{15}{4}}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>+</m>, <m>-</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">positive direction, slowing down</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\displaystyle {-\frac{9}{4}}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>-</m>, <m>-</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">negative direction, speeding up</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>\displaystyle {9}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>+</m>, <m>+</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">positive direction, speeding up</cell></row></tabular></p></solution>
    <answer><p>positive direction, slowing down</p></answer>
    <answer><p>negative direction, speeding up</p></answer>
    <answer><p>positive direction, speeding up</p></answer>
</stack-static>